<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT-SALOMON STARTS CONSUMER FINANCE COS.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-SALOMON STARTS CONSUMER FINANCE COS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Brothers said analyst Michael Durante started coverage of nine consumer finance companies.</p>
<p>-- Started MBNA Corp and AmeriCredit Corp with strong buy ratings.</p>
<p>-- Started Associates First Capital Inc, Beneficial Corp and Household International Inc with buy ratings.  </p>
<p>-- Started American Express Co, Capital One Financial Corp, Credit Acceptance Corp and Union Acceptance Corp with hold ratings.</p>
<p>-- In research note, Durante said he expected U.S. credit growth &quot;to slow going forward, testing quality growth for most consumer lenders.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Also said with industry consolidation underway, &quot;The best way to play is to buy the efficient consolidators and cherry-pick the few retail distribution rich targets.&quot;</p>
<p>((-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
</text>
